# Always install devDependencies, whatever NODE_ENV says.
#
# npm omits devDependencies when NODE_ENV=production, and that variable is set
# by more environments than people expect: CI images, container base images, and
# the agent runner that drives this repository all export it. The failure is
# confusing rather than obvious — `npm ci` succeeds, and then the ENTIRE vitest
# suite fails, because vitest itself is a devDependency. On a clean checkout of
# a green branch.
#
# Nothing here is deployed by npm: the dashboard ships as static files compiled
# into the Go binary. So there is no production install of this package to keep
# lean, and no reason to let an ambient variable decide what gets installed.
include=dev
